# Garage Go - Project Rules & Guidelines

## 📋 Project Overview

**Project Name:** Garage Go (Auto Garage Management System)  
**Type:** Full-stack ERP + CRM + Accounting System for Auto Garages  
**Architecture:** Clean Architecture (Domain-Driven Design)  
**Languages:** Dart (Backend), Flutter (Frontends), HTML/JS (Customer Frontend)  
**Database:** PostgreSQL with UUID primary keys

---

## 🎯 Core Principles

1. **Clean Architecture First:** Always follow the 4-layer architecture (Domain, Application, Infrastructure, Presentation)
2. **Null Safety:** Use `String?` for optional fields, always check for null before use
3. **Field Name Consistency:** Backend uses snake_case in DB, camelCase in entities. Frontend must handle both
4. **Pagination:** All list endpoints must support `page` and `limit` parameters
5. **Authentication:** All protected routes require JWT token in `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header
6. **Role-Based Access:** Use appropriate middleware for each route based on user role
7. **Error Handling:** Use unified Failure types and ErrorMiddleware for consistent error responses
8. **Database Transactions:** Use `runInTransaction` for multi-step operations
9. **Arabic UI:** All user-facing text must use app_localizations for Arabic/English support
10. **Audit Trail:** All critical operations must generate audit logs

---

## 📝 Code Style Guidelines

### Dart/Backend Code Style

```dart
// File naming: snake_case for files, camelCase for classes
// Example: booking_repository.dart, class BookingRepository

// Class naming: PascalCase
class BookingRepositoryImpl implements BookingRepository {
  // Private fields with underscore prefix
  final DatabaseConnection _db;
  
  // Constructor with dependency injection
  BookingRepositoryImpl(this._db);
  
  // Method naming: camelCase, descriptive
  Future<Booking> createBooking(CreateBookingParams params) async {
    // Always use async/await for async operations
    try {
      return await _db.runInTransaction(() async {
        // Transaction logic here
      });
    } catch (e) {
      throw ServerFailure('Failed to create booking');
    }
  }
}

// Entity naming: PascalCase, no suffix
class Booking {
  final String id;
  final String? customerId;  // Use ? for optional
  final DateTime createdAt;
  
  // Constructor with required and optional parameters
  Booking({
    required this.id,
    this.customerId,
    required this.createdAt,
  });
}

// Use extension methods for utilities
extension BookingExtension on Booking {
  bool get isPending => status == BookingStatus.PENDING;
}
```

### Flutter/Frontend Code Style

```dart
// Widget naming: PascalCase with Screen suffix for screens
class BookingsScreen extends ConsumerStatefulWidget {
  // Use ConsumerWidget/ConsumerStatefulWidget for Riverpod
  @override
  ConsumerState<BookingsScreen> createState() => _BookingsScreenState();
}

// Provider naming: camelCase with Provider suffix
final bookingsProvider = FutureProvider.autoDispose<List<Booking>>((ref) async {
  final apiService = ref.watch(apiServiceProvider);
  return await apiService.getBookings();
});

// Use const constructors where possible
const Text('Hello');

// Use trailing commas for multi-line parameters
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  return Scaffold(
    appBar: AppBar(
      title: Text('Bookings'),
    ),
    body: Consumer(
      builder: (context, ref, child) {
        final bookings = ref.watch(bookingsProvider);
        // ...
      },
    ),
  );
}
```

