## 🔐 Security Guidelines

### Authentication

- Use JWT tokens with 32+ character secret
- Implement token refresh mechanism
- Set appropriate token expiration (access: 15min, refresh: 7days)
- Use bcrypt for password hashing (cost factor: 10)
- Implement rate limiting for login (5 attempts/15min)

### Authorization

- Use role-based access control (RBAC)
- Role hierarchy: OWNER > MANAGER > ACCOUNTANT > RECEPTIONIST > MECHANIC
- Always validate permissions on both frontend and backend
- Use middleware for route protection

### Data Protection

- Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, API keys)
- Use environment variables for secrets
- Implement CORS with specific origins
- Validate all input on both client and server
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection

